{"title":"2006 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 9","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1_(Alcumus_Edition)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1 (Alcumus Edition)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Solution_5_(Forward_Casework_+_Listing)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 5 (Forward Casework + Listing)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>How many even three-digit integers have the property that their digits, all read from left to right, are in strictly increasing order? \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/8/9/58953c5fd0ee1618c795da0b5488d9c83ff62f2b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text {(A) } 21 \\qquad \\text {(B) } 34 \\qquad \\text {(C) } 51 \\qquad \\text {(D) } 72 \\qquad \\text {(E) } 150$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"384\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_1_.28Alcumus_Edition.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1_(Alcumus_Edition)\">Solution 1 (Alcumus Edition)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1 (Alcumus Edition)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let the integer have digits <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" />, read left to right. Because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/5/6/0560e859e3df4fe1a7d65338316b5d8feb6d42df.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1 \\leq a&lt;b&lt;c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"107\" height=\"15\" />, none of the digits can be zero and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> cannot be 2. If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/3/c63e18205b2a13c9f8d283e834e0bb8d145ba305.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c=4$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"41\" height=\"12\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> must each be chosen from the digits 1, 2, and 3. Therefore there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/e/36e78f0fbdcd23c47249963b83f7b45dc109adb4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\binom{3}{2}=3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -22px\" width=\"70\" height=\"53\" /> choices for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" />, and for each choice there is one acceptable order. Similarly, for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/b/4eb76404ee79952dcc555464b061509299789b09.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c=6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"43\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/3/fa39557a4d886b45466417ae28c5b0a3a92ba7ef.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c=8$\" width=\"40\" height=\"12\" /> there are, respectively, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/e/5/ee559317aed18491b8093c9dffcc7931e41f1991.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\binom{5}{2}=10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -22px\" width=\"79\" height=\"53\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/f/3/1f3a9f117a17b1ad4bbfb7f3ceb8f6ae31083c20.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\binom{7}{2}=21$\" style=\"vertical-align: -22px\" width=\"78\" height=\"53\" /> choices for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" />. Thus there are altogether <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/3/c/13cbbd387724d4a198f766a4d20f9862fde77b5b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3+10+21=\\boxed{34}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"144\" height=\"23\" /> such integers.\n</p><p><br />\n</p><p>(Edited by HMSSONI82)\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let's set the middle (tens) digit first. The middle digit can be anything from 2-7 (If it was 1 we would have the hundreds digit to be 0, if it was more than 7, the ones digit cannot be even).\n</p><p>If it was 2, there is 1 possibility for the hundreds digit, 3 for the ones digit.\nIf it was 3, there are 2 possibilities for the hundreds digit, 3 for the ones digit.\nIf it was 4, there are 3 possibilities for the hundreds digit, and 2 for the ones digit,\n</p><p>and so on.\n</p><p>So, the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/e/e/eee1c8834dddb06c9785230dd14c1068a8a6db7d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3(1+2)+2(3+4)+1(5+6)=\\boxed{34} \\Rightarrow B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"331\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The last digit is 4, 6, or 8.\n</p><p>If the last digit is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />, the possibilities for the first two digits correspond to 2-element subsets of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/7/9/d79ec62244f5a7fbd9d64230647971919bc40011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\{1,2,\\dots,x-1\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"125\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p>Thus the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/6/e3620f5a08ccdaee9a0ac9437e9fa75ed2b3db61.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"${3\\choose 2} + {5\\choose 2} + {7\\choose 2} = 3 + 10 + 21 = \\boxed{34}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -22px\" width=\"324\" height=\"53\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4\">Solution 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The answer must be half of a triangular number (evens and decreasing/increasing) so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/0/e50e5cb367b17bf9bfd57c6d08232a99a25484b3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{34}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"30\" height=\"23\" /> or the letter B.\n-\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_5_.28Forward_Casework_.2B_Listing.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_5_(Forward_Casework_+_Listing)\">Solution 5 (Forward Casework + Listing)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 5 (Forward Casework + Listing)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Casework:\n</p><p>For the sake of simplicity, we are going to call the number <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/5/d/c5d6cf4e9d072fbeba4fb13dffe63fa9ca820854.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{abc}$\" width=\"25\" height=\"16\" />.\n</p><p>1. If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/2/502e059d1a020b368aee3a99c5669d88331d321f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"45\" height=\"14\" />:\n</p><p>a. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/7/4f72da4187cb0ff8d0471bef17474df62fe69c94.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c=2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"43\" height=\"14\" />. No such number exists.\n</p><p>b. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/3/c63e18205b2a13c9f8d283e834e0bb8d145ba305.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c=4$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"41\" height=\"12\" />. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/6/2/a6228e534c6b824017479367bdbf354b9d3062de.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b=2, 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"60\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p>c. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/b/4eb76404ee79952dcc555464b061509299789b09.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c=6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"43\" height=\"14\" />. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/6/0d67aa4743edc663a9bce615c34628267de200fb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b=2, 3, 4, 5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"94\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p>d. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/3/fa39557a4d886b45466417ae28c5b0a3a92ba7ef.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c=8$\" width=\"40\" height=\"12\" />. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/b/f/cbfe0dc97f6e1e46412e3fe6a708cdafd7c09331.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b=2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"129\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p>2. If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/a/55afdab16c8c49089c4d9ceeb8d3c8cf1f088be6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a=2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"45\" height=\"14\" />: continue as above.\n</p><p>We can count up that there are 34 such integers, so select <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/e/f2e33ab9a00e021af49e888212645d4667903c49.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{B}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"26\" height=\"24\" />.\n</p><p>~hastapasta\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"2\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_12B\" title=\"2006 AMC 12B\">2006 AMC 12B</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_12B_Problems\" title=\"2006 AMC 12B Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_12B_Answer_Key\" title=\"2006 AMC 12B Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2006 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 8\">Problem 8</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2006 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 10\">Problem 10</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"2\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2006 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2006 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2006 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2006 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2006 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2006 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2006 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2006 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2006 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2006 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2006 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2006 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2006 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2006 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 15\">15</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_16\" title=\"2006 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 16\">16</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_17\" title=\"2006 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 17\">17</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_18\" title=\"2006 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 18\">18</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_19\" title=\"2006 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 19\">19</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_20\" title=\"2006 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 20\">20</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_21\" title=\"2006 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 21\">21</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_22\" title=\"2006 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 22\">22</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_23\" title=\"2006 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 23\">23</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_24\" title=\"2006 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 24\">24</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_25\" title=\"2006 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 25\">25</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"2\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AMC_12_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AMC 12 Problems and Solutions\"> All AMC 12 Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017160542\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.041 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.059 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 281/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 2296/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 156/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 6301/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   13.993      1 -total\n 59.26%    8.292      1 Template:AMC12_box\n 39.25%    5.492      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:2320:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017160542 and revision id 218878. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}